##RenderMan RIB-Structure 1.0
# GitHub issue #1 regression: random()/urandom() were missing from the JIT
# emitter's kHandledOpcodes dispatch table, so calls silently no-op'd under
# --jit/.slo (see random_probe.sl). numthreads 1 is required here, unlike
# the other spec-011/012 probes: those compute a deterministic function of
# (u,v), so which thread services a given micropolygon never matters, but
# this probe's *output is itself* raw random() draws -- with multiple
# threads, run-to-run bucket-to-thread scheduling is not fixed, so a given
# shading point can be serviced by a different thread (and therefore a
# different independently-seeded urand() stream) on each run. Confirmed
# empirically: two interpreter-only renders of this scene with the default
# thread count differed by MaxBlockAvgDiff 163 against each other; forced
# to a single thread, two runs are bit-identical (diff 0.00).
version 3.03
Hider "reyes"
Option "shaderformat" "default" ["rslo"]
Option "limits" "numthreads" [1]
Display "sphere-random-reyes.tif" "file" "rgba"
Projection "perspective"
Clipping 0.1 100
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
  Surface "random_probe"
  Sphere 1 -1 1 360
WorldEnd
